{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>At the end of three years.</b> This is the third tithe, and in this year he does not bring out second tithe. And some say that he brings out all three. And the disputants said that the commandment of תעשר is the first tithe." "And the sense of <b>and you shall bind up the silver in your hand</b>: he speaks with the Levite. And likewise, 'and the firstborn of your herd' — he speaks with the priest. And there is no second tithe except this one, which is for three years." "<b>At the end.</b> The beginning. And this tithe of three years is called poor man's tithe, and we rely on the tradition of our fathers."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:28.543516110Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}